  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d01fd2d64a9249049aaa77d5c12a82fe, type: 3}
  m_Name: Question 6
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  questionText: 6. You are given two screw gauges, one with a pitch of 0.5 mm and
    the other with a pitch of 1 mm, both having the same number of circular scale
    divisions. Which one is more accurate?
  referenceImage: {fileID: 0}
  explanationText: 'Screw gauge with less least count will be more accurate.

    Least
    count = pitch / (Number of divisions on the circular scale)

    As both the
    scales have the same number of circular scale divisions so the least count is
    directly

    proportional to the pitch of the screw gauge.

    The screw gauge
    with 0.5 mm pitch is more accurate.'
  options:
  - 'One with the pitch of 0.5 mm '
  - ' One with the pitch of 1 mm '
  - ' Both will give the same accuracy '
  - ' Information is insufficient'
  correctOptionIndex: 0
